{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>How they are bewildered</b> — like: <i>they are bewildered</i>, for the holem comes under the vav. <i>נבוכו</i> is on the pattern of <i>נכונו</i> (they are established), a pun for mockers: judgments." "<b>Are ashamed</b> — like: <i>תאשם שומרון</i> (Shall Shomron be held guilty) [Hosea 10:2]."], :book :joel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The phrase 'a pun for mockers: judgments' is cryptic; Ibn Ezra appears to be saying the similar-sounding forms create a wordplay, but the argument is compressed and the exact sense is uncertain. The citation behind the comparison to נכונו is unclear; no source matching this form was identified."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Joel -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/yoel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:06:26.983782628Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}